WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.680
Happy Monday, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, daily episode 469. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:16.600
Today is May 11th, 2026. A new week and plenty happening with Tesla. Tesla's final Model S and

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:23.560
Model X have left the Fremont line, freeing factory space for higher volume production as the company

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:30.340
moves on from its oldest platforms. Production of both models has ended at the Fremont factory

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:37.240
after 14 years for the Model S and 11 years for the Model X. The last units rolled off the line

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:42.860
and cleared assembly capacity that can now be redirected toward current high demand vehicles.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.280
This also marks the close of an era for Tesla's original flagship sedans and SUVs that help

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:57.280
define the brand. From a manufacturing standpoint, the decision makes sense because low volume platforms

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.640
were occupying valuable line space that higher volume models can use more efficiently.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.120
The shift reflects changing demand patterns where newer vehicles now drive most of the production needs.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.440
It is a practical move that lets the factory focus resources where they deliver the most output

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.440
with factory resources now focused on today's priorities. The end of these legacy platforms also

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.420
challenges the assumption that older models must stay in the lineup to preserve brand heritage or

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:35.020
factory flexibility. Production data shows the two models together accounted for a shrinking share

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:41.800
of output in recent years, while Fremont's lines have been reconfigured multiple times for higher volume

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:47.940
vehicles. This ratio matters because each freed station can support several times the

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:54.760
annual volume of the low volume flagships they replace. Tesla's vertical integration playbook suggests

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:00.580
the freed capacity will accelerate output of current models and upcoming variants rather than

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:07.940
sitting idle. The approach lets the company match factory resources more closely to actual demand curves

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:15.560
across its portfolio. While charging improvements help long distance travel, Tesla is also refining the

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:22.180
ownership experience for existing drivers through a new supercharger waitlist feature. The new virtual

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:28.440
queue system is now running at five supercharger sites and will roll out more broadly to manage

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:35.100
vehicle sequencing during busy periods. It directly tackles congestion that has frustrated drivers

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:42.140
at high traffic locations across the network. Early testing focuses on busy corridors where sequencing

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.960
issues have been most noticeable. This improves the practical experience for existing owners while

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:54.420
supporting continued growth in the EV fleet. Successful expansion could make the network more

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.960
predictable for long distance travel by reducing idle time and improving charger utilization.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:07.080
The pilot shows Tesla responding to real-world usage patterns rather than just adding more stalls.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:14.660
From an operations view, the feature addresses a growing pain point as more vehicles share the same

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:20.660
charging infrastructure. That same software stack is also pushing boundaries on the road itself

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:27.500
with a record cross-country drive. A Tesla completed the cross-country trip from New York to Los Angeles

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:35.200
on FSD supervised with zero interventions. The drive demonstrates the system's ability to handle varied

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:41.560
highway and urban conditions over thousands of miles. It provides fresh real-world data that can

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:47.380
refine future versions of the software. The zero intervention result highlights progress in

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:53.560
managing mixed environments without driver input. This kind of long distance validation matters because

00:03:53.560 --> 00:04:00.360
it tests the software under conditions that short tests cannot replicate. The data collected will likely

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:08.000
feed into the next iterations as engineers review edge cases from the route. That same software stack is

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.200
also heading to another major market with updates to Chinese owner's manuals. Updates to Chinese owner's

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:21.560
manuals indicate the latest full-self-driving software will launch for local drivers under a localized

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:28.120
name. The rollout would bring advanced driver assistance features to one of Tesla's largest markets.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:34.820
It also aligns with ongoing regulatory progress in the region that has been developing over recent

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:41.260
months. The move positions Tesla to offer its most current supervised capabilities in a key growth

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:47.480
area. Localizing the name reflects an effort to fit within regional expectations while delivering

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:54.000
the core technology. This kind of market-specific adaptation shows how the company is scaling its

00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:00.620
software beyond North America. Meanwhile, on the commercial side, Tesla is seeing fresh orders for

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:08.700
its heavy-duty truck. Watt EV placed an order for 370 Tesla semis, with more than 300 units slated

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:14.920
for a joint program with the port of Oakland. The deal follows the start of high-volume production

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:20.980
at the Nevada factory. Its signals growing commercial interest in electric long haul trucking,

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:27.860
as operators look for alternatives to diesel. A large portion of the order is earmarked for port-related

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:34.240
operations where emissions and efficiency targets are tightening. The timing aligns with increased

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:41.300
output capacity that can now support larger fleet commitments. This order adds concrete evidence

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:48.780
that electric semis are moving from pilot projects into broader adoption. The efficiency numbers behind

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:54.960
those trucks are also drawing attention from fleet planners. The Tesla semis efficiency claims

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:00.460
suggests it could circle the globe with roughly 80 charging stops under ideal conditions.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.960
The figure underscores the truck's potential range and energy use compared with diesel equivalents.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:13.020
It offers a concrete benchmark for fleet operators evaluating electric long haul options

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:20.300
and their total operating costs. The comparison helps illustrate why some operators are placing larger

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:27.460
orders as production scales. Real-world efficiency data like this can influence decisions on depot

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:33.540
charging infrastructure and route planning. Back at the consumer level, smaller but practical

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:39.980
software updates continued to land with improved smart summon. The updated software lets a Tesla

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:46.460
navigate parking lots and come pick up its owner more reliably than before. Owners can now summon

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:51.640
the car from farther away with better obstacle avoidance during the pickup process.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:59.120
The improvement shows how incremental FSD updates continue to expand everyday convenience features.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.920
These changes build on the same supervised stack that handled the recent cross-country drive.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:12.760
For daily use, the added distance and avoidance capability reduces the need for owners to walk across

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:19.620
large lots. It is another example of how ongoing releases refine the ownership experience without

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:26.140
